I take a taxi.
"Hello," the driver says.
"Where are you going?" he asks.
"I am going to Nyvej twelve," I answer.
We drive.
"Are you new in Copenhagen?" he asks.
"Yes, I am from Mexico," I say.
"The city is big," he says and smiles.
"Yes, very big," I answer.
I look out the window.
From the car I see the streets.
The houses are tall.
